('app_951c3317', 20, 'Test 6', NULL, NULL, '1_STRONG_HIRE_Aisyah_Rahman.pdf', 'Aisyah Rahman\nHR Executive\nPetaling Jaya, Selangor, MY  | +60 12 345 6721  | aisyah.rahman@fictionalmail.com  | \nlinkedin.com/in/aisyahrahman-demo\nSUMMARY\nHR Executive with 4 years of hands-on experience supporting the full employee lifecycle for a mid-sized services\ncompany in Malaysia. Comfortable managing recruitment coordination, onboarding, training logistics, HR records,\npayroll administration support, and employee relations with discretion and professionalism. Solid working knowledge\nof the Malaysian Employment Act 1955 and PDPA requirements.\nSKILLS\nFull Employee Lifecycle Administration  | Recruitment Coordination & Preliminary Interviews  | Onboarding &\nOffboarding  | Training & Development Coordination  | HR Records & PDPA Compliance  | Payroll Administration\nSupport  | Malaysian Employment Law  | HRMS (BrioHR)  | Microsoft Office (Excel, Word, PowerPoint)  | Employee\nRelations  | Event & Engagement Coordination\nEXPERIENCE\nHR Executive — Cempaka Business Solutions Sdn. Bhd.\nPetaling Jaya, Selangor  | Mar 2021 – Present\n Support the full employee lifecycle for a 180-staff organisation, including recruitment, onboarding, training\ncoordination, and offboarding.\n Draft job descriptions and job postings, and conduct preliminary phone/in-person interviews before shortlisting\ncandidates to hiring managers.\n Maintain employee records in BrioHR and ensure filing practices comply with PDPA requirements.\n Coordinate monthly training sessions and quarterly team-building/engagement events for the company.\n Assist the Finance team with payroll administration, verifying attendance, leave, and claims data each month for\n180 employees.\n Handle day-to-day employee queries on leave, benefits, and HR policy with empathy and confidentiality.\n Support HR compliance reviews to ensure adherence to the Employment Act 1955 and related regulations.\nHR Assistant — Melur Retail Group\nShah Alam, Selangor  | Jan 2019 – Feb 2021\n Provided administrative support to a 3-person HR team, including maintaining HR databases and physical filing\nsystems.\n Assisted with recruitment logistics — scheduling interviews, preparing offer letters, and coordinating new-hire\npaperwork.\nEDUCATION\nDiploma in Human Resource Management — Universiti Teknologi MARA (UiTM), 2018\nSijil Pelajaran Malaysia (SPM) — SMK Bukit Bintang, 2015\nCERTIFICATIONS\nCIPD Level 3 Foundation Certificate in People Practice', 'Aisyah Rahman\nHR Executive\nPetaling Jaya, Selangor, MY  | +60 12 345 6721  | [REDACTED EMAIL]  | \nlinkedin.com/in/aisyahrahman-demo\nSUMMARY\nHR Executive with 4 years of hands-on experience supporting the full employee lifecycle for a mid-sized services\ncompany in Malaysia. Comfortable managing recruitment coordination, onboarding, training logistics, HR records,\npayroll administration support, and employee relations with discretion and professionalism. Solid working knowledge\nof the Malaysian Employment Act 1955 and PDPA requirements.\nSKILLS\nFull Employee Lifecycle Administration  | Recruitment Coordination & Preliminary Interviews  | Onboarding &\nOffboarding  | Training & Development Coordination  | HR Records & PDPA Compliance  | Payroll Administration\nSupport  | Malaysian Employment Law  | HRMS (BrioHR)  | Microsoft Office (Excel, Word, PowerPoint)  | Employee\nRelations  | Event & Engagement Coordination\nEXPERIENCE\nHR Executive — Cempaka Business Solutions Sdn. Bhd.\nPetaling Jaya, Selangor  | Mar 2021 – Present\n Support the full employee lifecycle for a 180-staff organisation, including recruitment, onboarding, training\ncoordination, and offboarding.\n Draft job descriptions and job postings, and conduct preliminary phone/in-person interviews before shortlisting\ncandidates to hiring managers.\n Maintain employee records in BrioHR and ensure filing practices comply with PDPA requirements.\n Coordinate monthly training sessions and quarterly team-building/engagement events for the company.\n Assist the Finance team with payroll administration, verifying attendance, leave, and claims data each month for\n180 employees.\n Handle day-to-day employee queries on leave, benefits, and HR policy with empathy and confidentiality.\n Support HR compliance reviews to ensure adherence to the Employment Act 1955 and related regulations.\nHR Assistant — Melur Retail Group\nShah Alam, Selangor  | Jan 2019 – Feb 2021\n Provided administrative support to a 3-person HR team, including maintaining HR databases and physical filing\nsystems.\n Assisted with recruitment logistics — scheduling interviews, preparing offer letters, and coordinating new-hire\npaperwork.\nEDUCATION\nDiploma in Human Resource Management — Universiti Teknologi MARA (UiTM), 2018\nSijil Pelajaran Malaysia (SPM) — SMK Bukit Bintang, 2015\nCERTIFICATIONS\nCIPD Level 3 Foundation Certificate in People Practice', 'Review', 'Strong Hire', 91, 92, 90, 85, 'The uploaded document is a valid, well-structured resume for an HR Executive with 4 years of relevant experience. The candidate demonstrates strong alignment with nearly every core requirement in the job description, including full employee lifecycle support, recruitment coordination, payroll administration, and Malaysian employment law knowledge. Educational background meets the minimum requirement and is supplemented by a CIPD certification, a stated advantageous qualification. Overall this is a highly relevant and well-matched candidate for this role.', 'Diploma in Human Resource Management from UiTM (2018) and SPM from SMK Bukit Bintang (2015), supplemented by a CIPD Level 3 Foundation Certificate in People Practice.', '4 years of progressive HR experience, including current role as HR Executive at Cempaka Business Solutions handling full employee lifecycle, recruitment, payroll support, and compliance, preceded by an HR Assistant role at Melur Retail Group.', '[\"Recruitment Coordination\",\"Payroll Administration Support\",\"Malaysian Employment Law\",\"HRMS (BrioHR)\",\"Employee Relations\"]', '[\"Has direct experience supporting the full employee lifecycle from recruitment through offboarding.\",\"Demonstrates strong working knowledge of the Malaysian Employment Act 1955 and PDPA compliance requirements.\",\"Holds a CIPD Level 3 Foundation Certificate, matching the advantageous professional qualification mentioned in the job description.\",\"Has hands-on experience with payroll administration support, verifying attendance, leave and claims data.\",\"Shows experience coordinating training sessions and employee engagement events, directly matching stated responsibilities.\"]', '[\"Resume does not explicitly mention experience drafting or communicating formal HR policies and procedures beyond compliance reviews.\",\"No clear evidence of handling grievance or disciplinary case management, which often falls under employee relations responsibilities.\",\"Experience is limited to two organisations, so exposure to varied industries or larger-scale HR operations is not demonstrated.\"]', 'Strong Hire', 'Aisyah is a strong fit for this HR Executive role, bringing proven full-cycle HR experience, solid regulatory knowledge, and relevant certifications that align closely with the job description. Her background in a similarly sized organisation and hands-on payroll and compliance exposure make her well-suited to hit the ground running with minimal ramp-up time.', '1. Can you describe a specific instance where you helped draft or roll out a new HR policy and how you communicated it to employees? 2. Have you been involved in handling any employee grievance or disciplinary matters, and if so, how did you manage the process?', 1, '2026-08-21 03:32:39', 21, 'uploads/6a87c6cc6bf1a_1_STRONG_HIRE_Aisyah_Rahman.pdf', 'https://www.youtube.com/', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-21 03:32:39', 'None', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('app_9e739fda', 18, 'testing', NULL, NULL, '01_Marcus_Whitfield_CTO.pdf', 'Marcus Whitfield\nChief Technology Officer\nSingapore, SG  | +65 5512 4488  | marcus.whitfield@fictionalmail.com  | linkedin.com/in/marcuswhitfield-demo\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY\nTechnology executive with 18+ years leading engineering organizations for high-growth fintech and payments\ncompanies. Proven record scaling platforms from seed stage to IPO, building engineering cultures of 300+, and\ntranslating business strategy into resilient, secure technology roadmaps. Deep expertise in cloud-native architecture,\nplatform reliability, and cost-efficient scaling.\nCORE COMPETENCIES\nCloud Architecture (AWS/GCP)  | Engineering Leadership  | Platform Reliability (SRE)  | Fintech & Payments Systems\n | M&A; Technical Diligence  | Budget & P&L; Ownership  | Agile/DevOps Transformation  | Security & Compliance\n(PCI-DSS)\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\nChief Technology Officer — NovaLedger Financial Technologies\nSingapore  | Mar 2019 – Present\n Scaled engineering org from 40 to 320 across 6 countries while maintaining 99.98% platform uptime during 11x\ntransaction growth.\n Led migration from monolith to microservices on Kubernetes, cutting infrastructure cost per transaction by 42%.\n Built the technical due-diligence function for 4 acquisitions totaling USD 180M, integrating acquired platforms within\n90 days each.\n Established a company-wide SRE practice, reducing P1 incidents by 65% year-over-year.\nVP of Engineering — Quickpay Solutions Group\nHong Kong  | Jul 2014 – Feb 2019\n Directed 90-engineer division delivering core ledger and settlement systems processing USD 2.1B monthly volume.\n Introduced CI/CD pipeline adopted company-wide, reducing release cycle from 6 weeks to 3 days.\n Partnered with Compliance to achieve PCI-DSS Level 1 and ISO 27001 certification.\nDirector of Software Engineering — Bridgeway Systems Ltd.\nSydney, AU  | Jan 2009 – Jun 2014\n Managed 35-person engineering team building core banking middleware for 8 regional bank clients.\n Redesigned legacy batch-processing system into an event-driven architecture, cutting nightly reconciliation time\nfrom 5 hours to 40 minutes.\nEDUCATION\nM.S. in Computer Science — National University of Singapore, 2008\nB.Eng. in Information Systems — University of Melbourne, 2005\nCERTIFICATIONS\nAWS Certified Solutions Architect – Professional, Certified Kubernetes Administrator (CKA), PMP (Project\nManagement Professional)', 'Marcus Whitfield\nChief Technology Officer\nSingapore, SG  | +65 5512 4488  | [REDACTED EMAIL]  | linkedin.com/in/marcuswhitfield-demo\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY\nTechnology executive with 18+ years leading engineering organizations for high-growth fintech and payments\ncompanies. Proven record scaling platforms from seed stage to IPO, building engineering cultures of 300+, and\ntranslating business strategy into resilient, secure technology roadmaps. Deep expertise in cloud-native architecture,\nplatform reliability, and cost-efficient scaling.\nCORE COMPETENCIES\nCloud Architecture (AWS/GCP)  | Engineering Leadership  | Platform Reliability (SRE)  | Fintech & Payments Systems\n | M&A; Technical Diligence  | Budget & P&L; Ownership  | Agile/DevOps Transformation  | Security & Compliance\n(PCI-DSS)\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\nChief Technology Officer — NovaLedger Financial Technologies\nSingapore  | Mar 2019 – Present\n Scaled engineering org from 40 to 320 across 6 countries while maintaining 99.98% platform uptime during 11x\ntransaction growth.\n Led migration from monolith to microservices on Kubernetes, cutting infrastructure cost per transaction by 42%.\n Built the technical due-diligence function for 4 acquisitions totaling USD 180M, integrating acquired platforms within\n90 days each.\n Established a company-wide SRE practice, reducing P1 incidents by 65% year-over-year.\nVP of Engineering — Quickpay Solutions Group\nHong Kong  | Jul 2014 – Feb 2019\n Directed 90-engineer division delivering core ledger and settlement systems processing USD 2.1B monthly volume.\n Introduced CI/CD pipeline adopted company-wide, reducing release cycle from 6 weeks to 3 days.\n Partnered with Compliance to achieve PCI-DSS Level 1 and ISO 27001 certification.\nDirector of Software Engineering — Bridgeway Systems Ltd.\nSydney, AU  | Jan 2009 – Jun 2014\n Managed 35-person engineering team building core banking middleware for 8 regional bank clients.\n Redesigned legacy batch-processing system into an event-driven architecture, cutting nightly reconciliation time\nfrom 5 hours to 40 minutes.\nEDUCATION\nM.S. in Computer Science — National University of Singapore, 2008\nB.Eng. in Information Systems — University of Melbourne, 2005\nCERTIFICATIONS\nAWS Certified Solutions Architect – Professional, Certified Kubernetes Administrator (CKA), PMP (Project\nManagement Professional)', 'Review', 'Maybe', 58, 33, 80, 88, 'ATS Evaluation against Job Description requirements: Fulfills 33% of core required technical qualifications (AWS). Gaps noted for Python, Docker.', 'Tertiary Education / Diploma', '3+ Years Relevant Experience', '[\"AWS\"]', '[\"Directly matches mandatory Job Description skills: AWS [Resume Evidence: \\\"Chief Technology Officer\\\"].\",\"Documented background in relevant functional deliverables matching role requirements [Resume Evidence: \\\"Singapore, SG  | +65 5512 4488  | [REDACTED EMAIL]  | linkedin.com\\/in\\/marcuswhitfield-demo\\\"].\"]', '[\"Missing explicit documented experience for required Job Description skill(s): Python, Docker [Resume Evidence: Candidate resume contains 0 mentions of Python or Docker].\"]', 'Maybe', 'ATS Screener Note: Candidate brings partial alignment with key JD skills that require targeted technical interview probing.', '1. The job description requires experience with Python. Can you detail your actual working knowledge or equivalent experience with this requirement?\n2. How do your past accomplishments specifically prepare you for the main duties outlined in this job description?', 1, '2026-08-20 08:00:44', 14, 'uploads/6a86b42a5ab2c_01_Marcus_Whitfield_CTO.pdf', 'https://www.youtube.com/', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-20 08:00:44', 'None', NULL, NULL, NULL);
