('app_b0867fe8', 20, 'Test 8', NULL, NULL, '3_MAYBE_Michelle_Wong.pdf', 'Michelle Wong Mei Ling\nAdministrative Executive\nKuala Lumpur, MY  | +60 13 887 4402  | michelle.wong@fictionalmail.com  | linkedin.com/in/michellewong-demo\nSUMMARY\nAdministrative Executive with 5 years of experience running general office operations, vendor coordination, and\ncompany events for a professional services firm. Occasionally supports the HR team with new-hire paperwork and\nfiling, but has no dedicated recruitment, payroll, or employee-relations experience.\nSKILLS\nOffice Administration  | Vendor & Facilities Coordination  | Event Planning  | Filing & Documentation  | Microsoft Office\n(advanced Excel)  | Travel & Calendar Management  | Basic Data Entry\nEXPERIENCE\nAdministrative Executive — Anggerik Professional Services\nKuala Lumpur, MY  | Feb 2019 – Present\n Manage day-to-day office administration, vendor contracts, and facilities coordination for a 90-person office.\n Organise the firm\'s annual client appreciation event and internal staff celebrations.\n Occasionally assist the 2-person HR team with filing new-hire paperwork and updating personnel files during busy\nperiods.\nFront Desk & Admin Assistant — Teratai Hospitality Group\nKuala Lumpur, MY  | Jul 2016 – Jan 2019\n Handled front-desk operations, correspondence, and basic filing for a 30-person corporate office.\nEDUCATION\nDiploma in Office Management — Kolej Poly-Tech MARA, 2016', 'Michelle Wong Mei Ling\nAdministrative Executive\nKuala Lumpur, MY  | +60 13 887 4402  | [REDACTED EMAIL]  | linkedin.com/in/michellewong-demo\nSUMMARY\nAdministrative Executive with 5 years of experience running general office operations, vendor coordination, and\ncompany events for a professional services firm. Occasionally supports the HR team with new-hire paperwork and\nfiling, but has no dedicated recruitment, payroll, or employee-relations experience.\nSKILLS\nOffice Administration  | Vendor & Facilities Coordination  | Event Planning  | Filing & Documentation  | Microsoft Office\n(advanced Excel)  | Travel & Calendar Management  | Basic Data Entry\nEXPERIENCE\nAdministrative Executive — Anggerik Professional Services\nKuala Lumpur, MY  | Feb 2019 – Present\n Manage day-to-day office administration, vendor contracts, and facilities coordination for a 90-person office.\n Organise the firm\'s annual client appreciation event and internal staff celebrations.\n Occasionally assist the 2-person HR team with filing new-hire paperwork and updating personnel files during busy\nperiods.\nFront Desk & Admin Assistant — Teratai Hospitality Group\nKuala Lumpur, MY  | Jul 2016 – Jan 2019\n Handled front-desk operations, correspondence, and basic filing for a 30-person corporate office.\nEDUCATION\nDiploma in Office Management — Kolej Poly-Tech MARA, 2016', 'Review', 'Do Not Hire', 22, 20, 20, 30, 'The uploaded document is a legitimate resume, but the candidate\'s professional background is centered on general office administration rather than human resources. Her HR exposure is limited to occasional support tasks like filing new-hire paperwork, which falls far short of the recruitment, payroll, employee relations, and HR compliance responsibilities outlined in the job description. There is no evidence of proven HR role experience, HR systems proficiency, or knowledge of Malaysian employment law. Overall alignment with the core requirements of this HR Executive position is very weak.', 'Diploma in Office Management from Kolej Poly-Tech MARA, 2016. No HR-specific or professional HR certification (such as CIPD or SHRM) is listed.', '5 years as an Administrative Executive handling office operations, vendor coordination, and event planning, plus prior front desk/admin experience; HR involvement is limited to occasional filing support for a 2-person HR team.', '[\"Office Administration\",\"Vendor & Facilities Coordination\",\"Event Planning\",\"Filing & Documentation\",\"Microsoft Office (advanced Excel)\"]', '[\"Has experience organising company events and internal celebrations, which aligns with the JD\'s request for employee engagement activity support.\",\"Proficient in Microsoft Office, meeting one of the baseline technical requirements.\",\"Has some exposure to HR filing and personnel record updates, showing basic familiarity with HR documentation.\",\"Demonstrates strong administrative and organisational skills that could transfer to HR administrative support tasks.\"]', '[\"Resume explicitly states no dedicated recruitment, payroll, or employee-relations experience, which are core pillars of this role.\",\"No mention of any HR management systems or HRIS proficiency despite this being a listed requirement.\",\"No professional HR qualification such as CIPD or SHRM, and no evidence of knowledge in Malaysian employment law.\",\"No experience conducting interviews, coordinating hiring processes, or supporting HR compliance activities as required by the job description.\"]', 'Do Not Hire', 'Michelle\'s background is strongly administrative rather than HR-focused, and her resume self-identifies clear gaps in recruitment, payroll, and employee relations experience central to this role. She does not meet the proven HR role experience requirement and lacks any HR systems or employment law knowledge. She is not a suitable fit for this HR Executive position based on current qualifications.', '1. Can you describe any hands-on experience you have had with recruitment, payroll processing, or handling employee relations issues? 2. Are you familiar with any HR management systems or Malaysian employment legislation, and if so, can you provide specific examples?', 1, '2026-08-21 03:30:10', 30, 'uploads/6a87c63736aa3_3_MAYBE_Michelle_Wong.pdf', 'https://www.youtube.com/', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-21 03:30:10', 'None', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('app_c020e11a', 18, 'Test 4', NULL, NULL, '5_DO_NOT_HIRE_not_a_resume_recipe.pdf', 'Grandma Bea\'s Weekend Banana Bread\nIngredients: 3 ripe bananas, 1/3 cup melted butter, 3/4 cup sugar, 1 egg (beaten), 1 teaspoon vanilla\nextract, 1 teaspoon baking soda, pinch of salt, 1 1/2 cups all-purpose flour.\nInstructions: Preheat the oven to 350F (175C) and lightly grease a loaf pan. In a large bowl, mash the\nbananas with a fork until smooth. Mix in the melted butter, then the sugar, egg, and vanilla. Sprinkle\nthe baking soda and salt over the mixture and stir in. Add the flour last and mix until just combined; do\nnot overmix. Pour the batter into the prepared loaf pan and bake for 55-60 minutes, or until a\ntoothpick inserted in the center comes out clean. Let cool in the pan for 10 minutes before turning out\nonto a wire rack.\nNotes: For a richer flavor, swap half the butter for browned butter. Add a handful of walnuts or\nchocolate chips if desired. Store covered at room temperature for up to 3 days.', 'Grandma Bea\'s Weekend Banana Bread\nIngredients: 3 ripe bananas, 1/3 cup melted butter, 3/4 cup sugar, 1 egg (beaten), 1 teaspoon vanilla\nextract, 1 teaspoon baking soda, pinch of salt, 1 1/2 cups all-purpose flour.\nInstructions: Preheat the oven to 350F (175C) and lightly grease a loaf pan. In a large bowl, mash the\nbananas with a fork until smooth. Mix in the melted butter, then the sugar, egg, and vanilla. Sprinkle\nthe baking soda and salt over the mixture and stir in. Add the flour last and mix until just combined; do\nnot overmix. Pour the batter into the prepared loaf pan and bake for 55-60 minutes, or until a\ntoothpick inserted in the center comes out clean. Let cool in the pan for 10 minutes before turning out\nonto a wire rack.\nNotes: For a richer flavor, swap half the butter for browned butter. Add a handful of walnuts or\nchocolate chips if desired. Store covered at room temperature for up to 3 days.', 'Review', 'Do Not Hire', 0, 0, 0, 0, 'INVALID DOCUMENT REJECTED BY ATS: The uploaded file does not contain a standard candidate resume structure, work experience, or professional qualifications.', 'None / Not Provided', 'None / Not Provided', '[\"Invalid Document Format\"]', '[\"None - Invalid Document Format\"]', '[\"Uploaded document is not a valid candidate resume\\/CV [Resume Evidence: \\\"Grandma Bea\'s Weekend Banana Bread Ingredients: 3 ripe bananas, 1\\/3 cup melted butter, 3\\/4 cup sugar...\\\"]\",\"Fails mandatory ATS parsing and qualification standards.\"]', 'Do Not Hire', 'Automatically rejected by ATS screening due to non-resume file content.', '1. Please submit an official professional CV/Resume.\n2. Why was a non-resume document uploaded for this position?', 1, '2026-08-20 08:26:21', 19, 'uploads/6a86ba2b7d308_5_DO_NOT_HIRE_not_a_resume_recipe.pdf', 'https://www.youtube.com/', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-20 08:26:21', 'None', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('app_d212918b', 20, 'Test 10', NULL, NULL, '5_DO_NOT_HIRE_not_a_resume_pantry_guide.pdf', 'Simple Guide to Organising a Home Pantry\nStep 1: Empty the pantry completely and wipe down every shelf with a damp cloth. Check expiry\ndates on all items and discard anything that has gone bad.\nStep 2: Group similar items together — grains and pasta, canned goods, baking supplies, snacks,\nand spices. Clear, airtight containers work best for dry goods like rice, flour, and sugar since they\nkeep pests out and let you see at a glance when you\'re running low.\nStep 3: Store frequently used items at eye level and place heavier or rarely used items on the bottom\nor top shelves. Use small baskets or bins for loose packets so they don\'t get lost at the back.\nStep 4: Label each container and shelf so everyone in the household can find and return items to the\nright place. A simple printed label or masking tape and marker works fine.\nStep 5: Do a quick 10-minute tidy-up once a week and a full restock check once a month, noting\ndown anything that needs to be added to the next grocery list.', 'Simple Guide to Organising a Home Pantry\nStep 1: Empty the pantry completely and wipe down every shelf with a damp cloth. Check expiry\ndates on all items and discard anything that has gone bad.\nStep 2: Group similar items together — grains and pasta, canned goods, baking supplies, snacks,\nand spices. Clear, airtight containers work best for dry goods like rice, flour, and sugar since they\nkeep pests out and let you see at a glance when you\'re running low.\nStep 3: Store frequently used items at eye level and place heavier or rarely used items on the bottom\nor top shelves. Use small baskets or bins for loose packets so they don\'t get lost at the back.\nStep 4: Label each container and shelf so everyone in the household can find and return items to the\nright place. A simple printed label or masking tape and marker works fine.\nStep 5: Do a quick 10-minute tidy-up once a week and a full restock check once a month, noting\ndown anything that needs to be added to the next grocery list.', 'Review', 'Do Not Hire', 0, 0, 0, 0, 'INVALID DOCUMENT REJECTED BY ATS: The uploaded file does not contain a standard candidate resume structure, work experience, or professional qualifications.', 'None / Not Provided', 'None / Not Provided', '[\"Invalid Document Format\"]', '[\"None - Invalid Document Format\"]', '[\"Uploaded document is not a valid candidate resume\\/CV [Resume Evidence: \\\"Simple Guide to Organising a Home Pantry Step 1: Empty the pantry completely and wipe down every she...\\\"]\",\"Fails mandatory ATS parsing and qualification standards.\"]', 'Do Not Hire', 'Automatically rejected by ATS screening due to non-resume file content.', '1. Please submit an official professional CV/Resume.\n2. Why was a non-resume document uploaded for this position?', 1, '2026-08-21 01:46:56', 37, 'uploads/6a87ae0e60fa8_5_DO_NOT_HIRE_not_a_resume_pantry_guide.pdf', 'https://www.youtube.com/', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-21 01:51:36', 'None', NULL, NULL, NULL),
